# One line-ending policy for every text file, on every platform.
#
# The family's guards compare file CONTENT byte for byte in several places (layout sync, the
# bundle patches vs the roster, the README command-table pin in registry.spec.ts, the packaged
# payload). Without this file git checks text out with the platform's native endings: a Windows
# runner gets CRLF, splitting on LF leaves a trailing CR, and a spec that passes on Linux fails
# there — exactly what the windows-latest job caught. eol=lf makes the checkout identical.
* text=auto eol=lf
